<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Canada</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Canada is a country in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. Its eastern parts were settled as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>, the main North American colony of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>, until it was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a> and ceded in 1763. It then became part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> and developed into a self-governing dominion from 1867.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/canada.jpg" alt="Canada" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: George F. G. Stanley Modified by: The original uploader was Illegitimate Barrister at Wikimedia Commons. Th... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Canada_(Pantone).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
